      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "THE PUZZLE",
      "tone": "curious, playful",
      "narration_text": "Here's a puzzle from a textbook. Four squares in a row. Start on the left, reach the goal on the right, and every step costs a point. Two buttons, left and right. Easy. Except in the second square, the buttons are swapped. And you're blindfolded. Every square gives you the same reading, and you can't keep count of your steps. So whatever you do in one square, you do in all three. Which button do you press?",
