      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "THE PLAN",
      "tone": "warm, clear",
      "narration_text": "Hi, this is Tanmay Kulkarni, in for Humanitarians AI. This video is about one example from Sutton and Barto's Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction, a textbook about machines that learn by trial and error. Here's the key to the puzzle. Any rule you could pick is really a coin: how often it presses right, from never to always. So every answer gets a spot on this line, and a score. We'll try them one at a time. By the end you'll know the best answer. It isn't a button. It's a biased coin, set to one exact number.",
